24. Library access permissions and restrictions
The system must support configurable access policies.

Examples:

Active students can borrow books.

Registered lecturers can access staff borrowing privileges.

External members require approval.

Certain books are reference-only.

Some digital resources are limited to campus users.

Some subscribed resources require authenticated access.

Suspended members cannot borrow until the restriction is resolved.

Fee-related restrictions: Any policy that links borrowing privileges to financial clearance must be configurable, transparent and approved by the institution. It must not automatically block access to free library resources or override an authorized exception, appeal, welfare arrangement or other institutional policy.

A library access restriction should record:

